# Four-model prompt ablation on 50 fresh images

The user authorized testing each of four proposed prompt additions, checking overfitting and unrelated regressions, adding Claude Haiku 5.5 at low reasoning, and producing a 36-image original-photo collage with all four models' technical and aesthetic scores. This experiment evaluates agreement with frozen assistant assessments, not human accuracy. No labels are promoted to training.

## Fixed design

The previously reviewed 50 images and earlier trials informed the four hypotheses and are development evidence. Select 50 fresh views from 32 source families with seed 20261030, excluding previously exposed families, exact image hashes and conservative near duplicates. Match the previous mixture: six controlled families with parent plus three distortions (two blur, two noise, two JPEG), fourteen VizWiz and twelve standalone Megalith images. Preserve full-frame PNG views and a common maximum viewing scale within each controlled family. All routes and arms receive identical bytes. Results concern the delivered scale only.

Freeze arms.json, all six effective prompts, provider settings, analysis code, corpus manifest, blinded assistant references and this protocol before image inference. Each model sees the baseline and each single addition A/B/C/D plus their fixed combined version. The combined version always contains A+B+C+D in that order; there is no outcome-dependent selection, revision, second holdout search or retuning. This is 50 x 6 x 4 = 1,200 image requests, plus five text conformance probes per route. Each condition is sampled once, so within-condition stochastic variability is not separately estimated. Interleave arm order deterministically within each route.

A distinguishes recognizability from preserved fidelity and requires visible artifact signatures. B establishes the main focal region before weighting blur. C evaluates aesthetic cues by their whole-image contribution. D asks for anchor-first scoring with consistent concise evidence. These changes operationalize the previous recommendations; their effects remain hypotheses.

## Models and structured output

Use RunInfra deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 through its recorded API alias, no reasoning, temperature zero, max_tokens 2048; OpenRouter google/gemini-3.8-flash, medium reasoning, temperature zero; OpenRouter openai/gpt-6-luna, high reasoning, temperature omitted; and OpenRouter anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5, low native adaptive reasoning, temperature omitted. OpenRouter output budgets are 16384 inclusive of reasoning, with excluded reasoning text. Pin catalog-supported providers and disable fallbacks; require supported parameters. Do not substitute unavailable models or silently change reasoning settings.

Preserve the strict joint schema: exactly technical_quality and aesthetics, each containing task, status, score, evidence and limitations. Scores are enum strings from "1.00" through "5.00" in "0.10" steps or null with unscorable status. This spelling does not imply hundredth-point measurement precision. Evidence targets 12–20 words with a hard maximum of 30. Keep the original task constructs, null behavior and independent task validation. Do not repair invalid labels or average technical and aesthetic ratings together. Strict JSON validity does not establish visual accuracy.

Probe endpoints using the previous five exact score/status combinations before image calls. Log a durable request attempt before sending, retain raw replies, accepted identities, usage and returned provider information, and never automatically retry an uncertain or rejected request. Permit up to four concurrent calls per route subject to conservative budget admission, with a cap of $5 per route and $20 overall including probes. Unknown billing, transport uncertainty or provider/identity errors stop new calls on that route after draining admitted requests. Ordinary priced response-validation failures remain recorded and do not erase a valid sibling task. Key values remain outside artifacts and logs.

## Independent references and issue groups

Three fresh-context assistant reviewers inspect anonymous shuffled packets of 17/17/16 individual supplied images, using the original joint rubric. They see no model outputs, prompt additions, source metadata, scores or labels. Collect two point scores, plausible subjective uncertainty intervals and visible evidence per image. One reviewer assesses each case; inter-reviewer reliability is not measured. Freeze all reference files before inference. Reference intervals describe judgment uncertainty, not confidence intervals.

Record available source issue tags before predictions. They are metadata for analysis only and never enter model or reviewer prompts. Prespecified regression groups include source stratum, controlled operator and severity, clean parents, degraded variants, low references (<=2), high references (>=4), and available natural-image issue tags. For exploratory targeted/complement summaries, A targets degraded controlled JPEG/noise, B targets degraded controlled blur, and C uses VizWiz as an imperfect natural-image proxy; report that limitation. D addresses all cases. Always examine both dimensions, especially aesthetic spillover from A/B and technical spillover from C. Small subgroup counts can leave regressions unresolved.

## Analysis fixed before outcomes

For each route/arm/task report planned, attempted, valid, scorable and paired coverage; mean absolute error (MAE), signed bias, distance outside reference intervals, interval hits, large interval misses and critical contradictions. Critical contradictions are student >=4 with reference upper<=2, or student<=2 with reference lower>=4. Preserve errors and missing values. Compare each arm with its own model baseline on identical valid scorable cases; report missingness separately so improved MAE cannot conceal invalid outputs. Also report common-case comparisons where appropriate.

Positive observed impact means a lower paired MAE; negative means higher paired MAE; zero within numerical tolerance means unchanged. Report the actual signed change (arm minus baseline) and uncertainty, separately by task. Resample whole image families within source strata for 10,000 paired bootstrap draws with seed 20261030. The eight combined-versus-baseline comparisons (four routes x two tasks) are primary: report ordinary 95% intervals and Bonferroni 99.375% intervals. The 32 single-addition comparisons are exploratory with nominal 95% intervals; do not treat a nominal interval as multiplicity-adjusted confirmation. All inference is conditional on these references and selected families.

For each arm, report new critical contradictions, cases whose absolute error worsens by at least 0.5, invalid-task increases, and subgroup MAE increases above 0.10. Assess noninferiority against the prespecified 0.10 MAE margin using a one-sided 95% upper bound where paired groups allow it. A nonsignificant difference alone does not establish lack of harm. Do not promote a change solely because an aggregate improves while a relevant group or the other task degrades. Primary improvement requires a corrected upper interval below zero; report unresolved safety/regression groups honestly.

Controlled severity ordering and parent-to-severe score separation are technical diagnostics; operator strength is not human perceptual truth, and aesthetics need not decline monotonically. Increased score spread alone is not success. Report DeepSeek+Luna and all-four equal-weight averages per task as diagnostic ensembles, retaining their component predictions; agreement cannot exclude shared mistakes.

## Documentation and collage

Save complete per-case results, raw-output provenance, exact prompts, freeze hashes, provider settings and actual costs. Document positive, negative, unchanged or uncertain effects for every addition and model/task, including non-targeted failures and selection limitations. Use the fixed combined arm for the new 36-image collage regardless of which arm wins. Select all 32 families plus four severe variants using a prespecified rule, sort by reference technical score, and show each model's technical/aesthetic pair in the same order. Include the reference for context. Render the original scored image files without generative redrawing; full originals remain clickable. Clearly label the arm and reasoning settings. This avoids the loss of blur, grain and compression seen in the earlier generated preview.

